{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109803-initiative","id":1109803,"title":"Initiative","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-30T09:49:16-07:00","id":1109803,"title":"Initiative","content":"Mages, compared to vampires, werewolves and etc. have really small initiative rating. I mean, vampires can go above 20 (Celerity + Dexterity + Wits), and simple rank 2 Gift can throw werewolf past 30 or more. Now, I heard that there's a rote that combines Time 1 with Correspondence 1 to improve your initiative. How the system work? Is it as per damage chart? 1 successes per 2? I'd need rules for that. Also, if I'd want to cast permanent effect on myself, that'd be Time 1 Coresspondence 1 Life 3? What if I roll 15 succeses in total, spend 5 on duration and 10 on actual effect. Does that mean.<br /> I have dexterity 4 and wits 3, and I roll a die with 10. thats 17. Together with my effect, 17 + 20 is 37. Is that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T10:27:31-07:00","id":1109821,"title":"","content":"You seem to be exaggerating things a bit here. Without being fairly low Generation (aka while their caps are still 5s), a vampire's &quot;passive&quot; initiative maxes out at 15 + 1d10, They can relatively cheaply (depending on their Dex) get to 16 + 1d10. Pushing beyond that is rarely worth it (requires constantly spending blood on buffing Dexterity every turn, so it doesn't last long and denies you lots of other options). Spirit of the Fray for werewolves is kinda silly good in this department, but it isn't that overwhelming. Without Spirit of the Fray (or a few other potential boosts like the rare Totem that can boost an Attribute above 5), they cap out at 12 + 1d10 (and that assumes being in Hispo or Lupus, which has plenty of drawbacks outside of a white room). Spirit of the Fray does jump that to 22 + 1d10, but the option to go to 32 + 1d10 is idiotic without a Rank 5 Glasswalker Gift (Chaos Mechanics), and is like spending all your blood a bit of a trap. It requires spending Gnosis, which means for that turn you lose access to spending Rage for all the combat stuff it does, or spending Rage to activate lots of different combat Gifts.<br /> <br /> While not without drawbacks, mages can brute force their way into this level of initiative rather easily with just Life 3/Mind 1, as both allow you to boost the relevant Attributes. You don't want to walk around with 20 + 1d10 by boost your Dex and Wits to 10 each with magic because of things like Pattern Bleeding, but it's not exactly beyond a mage to do so. With Time 4 or Prime 3 you can make it easier by hanging the spell (so you can leave it with a duration short enough to not worry about the things designed to keep down long term high end magic), or have a combat power up single use Wonder to go crazy with.<br /> <br /> Any rotes about this are fan made, because the books have a long history of ignoring direct Initiative boosting in any of the sample spells. If you need rules for that... all you've got are the ones in the book for creating your own effects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T10:48:26-07:00","id":1109831,"title":"","content":"The only Rote I know of that uses a spell to directly add points to the next initiative roll is in the 2nd Ed Iteration X book, page 49, named &quot;Time-Motion Study.&quot;<br /> <br /> It uses Correspondence 1, Time 1 for the effect, and each success adds to the next initiative roll. Technically you could come up with a rote that uses the same spheres, but has a duration added to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:06:48-07:00","id":1109889,"title":"","content":"Thanks! You guys helped.me a lot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theo